      "artist": "Paul VanDerWerf from Brunswick, Maine, USA",
      "description": "A couple of establishments on Maine Street here in Brunswick, Me.  As the sign says this is intended to be a New York style deli.  I have not tried the pastrami on rye that to me along with corned beef or beef tongue are among the musts for an NY deli.  Lots of reflections here and was one reason I took the photo. \nFrom Yelp\nOne of the best delis in Maine. One of the only delis in Maine for that matter!\n\nGreat place to grab a sandwich in downtown Brunswick. Huge menu. They make a great Rueben. The Barnum, kind of a turkey Rueben with coleslaw instead of sauerkraut is my favorite sandwich there. Good selection of veggie options as well. Quality boar's head meats and cheeses and good drinks selection including Mexican Coke, the kind in a glass bottle.",
